target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestTailLimitKeepsTheNewestRows'
expect: the tail dropped the newest run
why:    taking the first n lines instead of the last makes every derived answer describe runs that have already scrolled away, while looking exactly as healthy. Re-anchored: the slice now also computes how many lines it dropped, so the error messages can name a FILE line number
--- old
		dropped = len(lines) - limit
		lines = lines[dropped:]
--- new
		dropped = len(lines) - limit
		lines = lines[:limit]
